# .gitattributes -- written Aug 7 2026, Eli.
#
# WHY: the first real commit of this repo (0c75bc0, four months of production
# work) threw ~32 "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it"
# warnings. Nothing was wrong -- Windows checkouts get CRLF by default, so a
# later checkout or pull could rewrite every one of those files and show them
# as modified when not one character of logic had changed. A diff that lies
# about what changed is the same disease as a count that lies about what it
# read, in a smaller costume.
#
# This normalises every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working
# copy. Vercel deploys the working copy, and CRLF vs LF is meaningless to Node,
# so this changes nothing that runs. It only makes `git status` honest.
#
# .cmd is deliberately excepted: Windows batch files are safer with CRLF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
